# Make clones deterministic across platforms.
#
# On macOS git applies `core.ignorecase = true` and `core.precomposeunicode =
# true` as DEFAULTS whenever they are unset — and on the canonical checkout
# they are unset: `git config --show-origin --get-all core.ignorecase` returns
# nothing and .git/config has no [core] section (measured 2026-09-01; this
# header used to say .git/config "sets" them, which it never did). The effect
# is the same either way: those are per-machine behaviours that do NOT travel
# with a clone, so a Linux checkout can disagree about path casing and Unicode
# normalisation with no error — the kind of difference that shows up as a
# phantom diff or a module that resolves locally and 404s in CI.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never normalise, never diff as text.
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.gif       binary
*.ico       binary
*.webp      binary
*.pdf       binary
*.woff      binary
*.woff2     binary
*.ttf       binary
*.jar       binary
*.keystore  binary

# Generated: 690 KB of Supabase types. Collapse it in diffs so a regen does not
# bury a real change, but keep it TRACKED and readable — CLAUDE.md rule 3 tells
# agents to read it, and .cursorignore was un-ignoring it for the same reason.
src/lib/types/database.ts linguist-generated=true

# Lockfile: same reasoning.
package-lock.json linguist-generated=true
